{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.md","line":194,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex#thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#def:pet-ch7-maximal-function]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-5]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","line":366,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[maximal-function weak estimate]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0303}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch7-maximal-function}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.1.14}\n  Assume $(M,g)$ has $\\Ric\\ge(n-1)k$. There is $C=C(n,kD^2)$ such that for all\n  $t>0$,\n  \\[\n    t\\,\\vol\\{M(u)>t\\}\\le C\\int|u|\\,\\vol.\n  \\]\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem,lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison,rem:pet-ch7-ex-5}\n  \\sketch\n  For each \\(x\\) with \\(M(u)(x)>t\\), choose \\(R_x\\) with \\(t\\vol B(x,R_x)<\\int_{B(x,R_x)}|u|\\). The covering lemma \\cref{rem:pet-ch7-ex-5} supplies disjoint \\(B(x_i,R_i)\\) whose fivefold enlargements cover the level set. Relative volume comparison and disjointness give \\(t\\vol\\{M(u)>t\\}\\le C\\int|u|\\).\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[maximal-function weak estimate] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368372d6d6178696d616c2d66756e6374696f6e2d7468656f72656d\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0303</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23def%3Apet-ch7-maximal-function\">↗ def:pet-ch7-maximal-function</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:7.1.14</span></span>Assume <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k$\">$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k$</span>. There is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C=C(n,kD^2)$\">$C=C(n,kD^2)$</span> such that for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t&gt;0$\">$t&gt;0$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  t\\, \\vol \\{ M(u)&gt;t\\} \\le C\\int |u|\\, \\vol .  \\]\">\\[  t\\, \\vol \\{ M(u)&gt;t\\} \\le C\\int |u|\\, \\vol .  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison\">↗ lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23rem%3Apet-ch7-ex-5\">↗ rem:pet-ch7-ex-5</a> \\sketch For each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M(u)(x)&gt;t$\">$M(u)(x)&gt;t$</span>, choose <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R_x$\">$R_x$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\vol B(x,R_x)&lt;\\int _{B(x,R_x)}|u|$\">$t\\vol B(x,R_x)&lt;\\int _{B(x,R_x)}|u|$</span>. The covering lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23rem%3Apet-ch7-ex-5\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-5\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368372d65782d35\">item 2</a> supplies disjoint <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B(x_i,R_i)$\">$B(x_i,R_i)$</span> whose fivefold enlargements cover the level set. Relative volume comparison and disjointness give <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\vol \\{ M(u)&gt;t\\} \\le C\\int |u|$\">$t\\vol \\{ M(u)&gt;t\\} \\le C\\int |u|$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#def:pet-ch7-maximal-function","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-weak-poincare-sobolev-estimate","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#def:pet-ch7-maximal-function","title":"def:pet-ch7-maximal-function","label":"def:pet-ch7-maximal-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/ch